      "content": "Regulations are frequently weaponized by entrenched corporate interests to maintain their market dominance. Large, established monopolies possess the legal and financial infrastructure to absorb the high costs of compliance, effectively turning regulatory burdens into exclusionary barriers. This allows them to strategically slow down or outright prevent nimble, innovative small businesses from gaining a foothold. Ultimately, these supposed safeguards become sophisticated tools for protecting existing power structures rather than ensuring fair competition.",
      "source": "target",
