      "content": "The notion that regulation can genuinely help small businesses is a deeply flawed premise when the current system is in place. While proponents claim consumer protection, these regulations are overwhelmingly designed to favor scale, which inherently benefits massive corporations. The system is fundamentally rigged because the compliance costs scale exponentially, creating an insurmountable moat around incumbents. True support for small business requires deregulation, not more bureaucratic oversight.",
